<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Cera Bank 1996 net profit soars 71.2 pc.</title>
<headline>Belgian Cera Bank 1996 net profit soars 71.2 pc.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in billions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		     5.779     vs   3.376</p>
<p>    Current pre-tax profit	    5.922     vs   3.974</p>
<p>NOTE - Unlisted Cera Bank is Belgium's sixth-largest bank.  </p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		  1,351.52	vs   1,209.91</p>
<p>    Client deposits			  807.78	vs     748.24</p>
<p>    Loans to clients			 428.38	vs     388.55</p>
<p>    Loans to the public sector	   332.75	vs     314.02</p>
<p>    Write-offs and provisions		4.79	vs	 4.74</p>
<p>    Operating costs and depreciation    18.39	vs	16.62</p>
<p>    Return on equity (in pct)	     11.84	vs	 7.58</p>
<p>    Risk asset ratio (in pct)	     12.38	vs	13.20</p>
<p>    Staff				    4,573	   vs   4,514</p>
<p>    Number of branches		     939	   vs     953</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815</p>
</text>
